<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Diaspora.Modules.Jobs</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Diaspora.Modules.Jobs</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The Jobs &amp; Careers Platform (Phase B9). The platform's single owner of employment:
      who is hiring, what they are hiring for, who applied, and what happened next.

      A job posting is not a classified advert. It belongs to a verified employer, moves through
      a lifecycle from draft to filled, carries a salary a candidate can compare across
      currencies, states plainly whether it sponsors a visa, and closes when the seat is taken.
      An application is not a form submission: it is a durable record with a complete, append-only
      history, a hiring pipeline behind it, interviews scheduled against it and an offer at the
      end. Both sides are first-class — the employer's dashboard and the candidate's dashboard
      read the same aggregates from opposite ends.

      What Jobs owns: postings, employers, candidates, applications, interviews, offers,
      pipelines, alerts, saved jobs and the employment catalogues. What it deliberately does not:
      the badge on an employer belongs to Trust, the country a job sits in belongs to Location,
      the résumé bytes belong to Media, the recruitment agency behind a posting belongs to
      Providers, the work-permit explainer beside it belongs to Guides, and the discussion under
      it belongs to Community. Jobs reaches every one of them through published contracts and
      stores identifiers, never copies.

      Search is a seam, not an engine: the module ships an EF-backed search over the write model
      and the IJobSearchEngine port an OpenSearch adapter can satisfy later without a domain
      change. Recommendations are a seam on the same terms, with a shipped heuristic and no
      matching model anywhere in the module. Categories, ranking and verification sources are
      contributor seams too.

      Registers entirely through B2.6 contributor interfaces: no edit to the Platform Kernel,
      the Identity module, Trust, Location, Media, Community, Providers, Guides, or Program.cs.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    B8's reference set plus B8 itself.

    Location, Media, Community, Providers and Guides are deliberate and documented. B9 consumes
    Location's published Integration and Extensibility contracts (IGeographicScopeResolver,
    INearbyResourceProvider, ILocationResourceCounter), Media's published reference contracts
    (attach-by-reference, never URLs — and MediaOwnerType.Job has existed since B5), Community's
    published Integration contracts (ICommunityBookmarkService, ICommunityCommentService,
    ICommunityModerationService, ICommunityContentSource — and CommunityContentType.Job has
    existed since B6), Providers' published IProviderDirectory for the recruitment agencies and
    career coaches behind a posting, and Guides' published IGuideDirectory and IGuideCatalog for
    the contextual work-permit and interview guides beside one.

    Notably absent: the Identity module and the Trust module. Jobs reaches Identity through the
    kernel's ICurrentUser and Trust through Diaspora.Contracts — the published
    ITrustVerificationSubmission contract and Trust's published integration events — never
    through their aggregates. An architecture test enforces both.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.SharedKernel\Diaspora.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Contracts\Diaspora.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Platform\Diaspora.Platform.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Application\Diaspora.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Persistence\Diaspora.Persistence.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Location\Diaspora.Modules.Location.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Media\Diaspora.Modules.Media.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Community\Diaspora.Modules.Community.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Providers\Diaspora.Modules.Providers.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Guides\Diaspora.Modules.Guides.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
